2. Read the document section to be classified
3. Compare the section content against ALL standards and subspecifications in the specification
4. Identify the SINGLE BEST matching standard (1-21) and subspecification (a-f)
5. If the content clearly relates to a specific standard but you cannot determine the exact subspecification, provide your best match
6. If the content does not relate to any CSHSE standard (e.g., table of contents, acknowledgments, general administrative content), mark it as "unmatched"

You MUST provide a detailed rationale explaining WHY this section matches (or doesn't match) the specification. Reference specific language from BOTH the section AND the specification that supports your decision.`;

// User message with the FULL spec and the section to classify
const userMessage = `=== COMPLETE CSHSE SPECIFICATION DOCUMENT ===

${fullSpecContent}

